#ASSERT `s 270.1(3) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `by indictment` `s 270 test: the s 787(1) general penalty` EQUALS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
#ASSERT `s 270.1(3) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `on summary conviction` `s 270 test: the s 787(1) general penalty` EQUALS `s 270 test: the s 787(1) general penalty`

§ `s 270.03: the court's duty as a regulative rule (run with #TRACE; a DEONTIC value cannot be asserted on the stable binary)`

-- TRACE-EXPECT: MUST `s 270.03 the court directs
-- (the text states no time limit, so the duty stands until performed: the trace prints the standing obligation, not a breach)
#TRACE `s 270.03 the sentencing court's duty to direct consecutive service` `s 270.03 test: s 270(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 5
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 270.03 the sentencing court's duty to direct consecutive service` `s 270.03 test: s 270(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 270.03 the court directs that the sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment` AT 3
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 270.03 the sentencing court's duty to direct consecutive service` `s 270.03 test: s 270.1(1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 5
